# CLAUDE.md Template

Copy this template when creating root `CLAUDE.md` in a target repository. Keep it as a table of contents that points to configured docs paths. Create `AGENTS.md -> CLAUDE.md` so AGENTS.md readers see the same map.

```markdown
# CLAUDE.md

This file is the repository-level rule map for agent context. The harness source of truth is this plugin's docs-adjacent metadata file at `docs/harness-engineering/harness-engineering.json`. Update the referenced docs and scripts instead of adding long guidance here.

## Harness Config

See `docs/harness-engineering/harness-engineering.json` for docs paths, scripts paths, checks, staged gates, CI provider, and hooks.

## Guardrails

See `docs/harness-engineering/guardrails.md` for setup-time repository guardrails and scoped path rules.

## Readiness

See `docs/harness-engineering/readiness.md` for maturity level, known violations, ratchet budget, and doc freshness status.

## Harness Updates

See `docs/harness-engineering/updates.md` for guardrail changes and docs/script alignment records.

## Architecture

See `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the target repository's source roots, layer model, allowed dependencies, ADR constraints, profile-specific rules, and architecture checks.

## Full Specs

See `docs/product-specs/` for durable product, feature, and system specifications. Implementation changes should update the relevant spec and validation script together.

## Generated Docs

See `docs/generated/` for derived artifacts with provenance, source paths, and regeneration commands. Source schemas stay in checked-in project roots such as migrations, OpenAPI/protobuf/GraphQL specs, or Prisma schema.

## Active Work

See `docs/exec-plans/active/` for in-progress execution plans.

## Completed Work

See `docs/exec-plans/completed/` for completed execution plans and decision logs.

## Quality And Debt

See `docs/QUALITY_SCORE.md` and `docs/exec-plans/tech-debt-tracker.md` for quality tracking and known follow-up work.

## Validation

Run `sh scripts/harness/validate_harness.sh` before changing harness docs, scripts, CI, hooks, or architecture rules. The wrapper must execute Python only through `uv run`; provision `uv` before running validation.

Every harness configuration, validation script, wrapper command, CI/hook template, and allowed command form is a lifecycle artifact. When the project matures, update the harness config, scripts, CI, and hooks together and keep them documented and validated as a unit.

## References

See `docs/references/` for third-party or generated reference material packaged for offline agent use.
```

## Symlink setup

```bash
ln -s CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md
mkdir -p .agents .claude/skills
ln -s ../.claude/skills .agents/skills
```

Use `.agents/skills -> ../.claude/skills` only after creating `.agents/` and `.claude/skills`. Do not maintain duplicate skill inventories. `AGENTS.md` should remain a symlink to `CLAUDE.md`, not a separate instruction file.
